  "$comment": "Fixture spec for the tiered-mount-pool read-differential (W4.1d batch 3a). Two characters (A responding, B participant) baked via the REAL repos.characters.create (each mints a linked vault mount, read back by the builder + oracle); a group G1 with an official store + a linked store + charA membership (NOT charB — proves the per-RESPONDING-character group tier); a project P1 with two linked stores PLUS colliding links to charA-vault / G1-official / the General store (proves the character>group>global dedup drops them from project); and the Quilltap General singleton whose id lives in the MAIN db instance_settings. All store/group/project/user ids are pinned so the resolved pools compare with ZERO normalization (the char-vault mounts are minted but pinned by read-back on both sides). P4.D231 (v4 08c49319d): `helperPlants` (applied to BOTH work copies before anything reads them — new groups with no members, so the matrix is untouched) and `helperArms` drive the NEW `resolveMountPointIdsForGroup` directly.",
