  "$p4d376Comment": "P4.D376 (v4 `0c47f4539`, pin `624d0d25c`): the builder bakes four projects through v4's REAL `repos.projects.create` (each mints + links its official store): Roster Hall (allowAnyCharacter false, roster [charA], plus projectStoreA linked), Unlinked Official (its official link DELETED, projectStoreB linked — the official store is NOT linked), Late Official (the official link deleted, projectStoreA linked, then the official re-linked — linked AFTER another store), Disabled Links (a disabled store and a mount id with NO row linked). Character C (Cora) is baked with her vault DISABLED and is the one member of group G-DIS (official store disabled, one enabled linked store). Every `matrix` row states `roster` / `enabled` explicitly (the pre-existing nine `open` / `ignore` — what v4's `{}` meant at the baseline; at the pin an `{}` would leave both `undefined`, which is neither `gated` nor `require`, so the output is the same), may carry `before` / `after` SQL on the mount index (the disabled-General row), and records the pool's own log lines (`logs`, `poolLog` messages only). `groupedArms` gain `includeEmpty`; `projectTierArms` gain the official-first rows.",
